Subject: [PATCH] Server: accept a responseEncoding, as Client already does

`Client` takes a `responseEncoding` and hands it to its `Deserializer`, which
has taken an `encoding` argument since the beginning. `Server` does not: it
constructs `new Deserializer()` with no arguments, so an incoming `event`,
`newDevices` or `setReadyConfig` whose payload carries a non-ASCII string is
decoded as UTF-8 and mangled - the same bug the client option exists to fix, on
the other side of the connection.

The CCU's interface processes speak ISO-8859-1 and their XML carries no encoding
declaration, so the deserializer cannot work it out on its own; only the caller
knows. In practice a callback payload is addresses, datapoint names and numbers,
so nothing has been observed in the wild - but a device name in a `newDevices`
answer or a string datapoint in an `event` is enough, and there is currently no
way to ask for the right encoding.

The change keeps the default (`utf8`, from `Deserializer`), so nothing that
exists behaves differently. `xmlrpc.createServer(options)` passes the whole
options object through, so `responseEncoding` needs no plumbing of its own.

Verified against homematic-xmlrpc 2.0.0.

---
 lib/server.js | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/server.js b/lib/server.js
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/lib/server.js
+++ b/lib/server.js
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@
  *                                  with fields:
  *   - {String} host              - (optional)
  *   - {Number} port
+ *   - {String} responseEncoding  - (optional) encoding of incoming request
+ *                                  bodies; 'utf8' by default, 'latin1' for a CCU
  * @param {Boolean} isSecure      - True if using https for making calls,
  *                                  otherwise false.
  * @param {Function} onListening  - (optional) called once listening
@@ -35,6 +37,8 @@ function Server(options, isSecure, onListening) {
   onListening = onListening || function() {}
   var that = this

+  var responseEncoding = (options && options.responseEncoding) || 'utf8'
+
   // If a string URI is passed in, converts to URI fields
   if (typeof options === 'string') {
     options = url.parse(options)
@@ -49,7 +53,7 @@ function Server(options, isSecure, onListening) {
   }

   function handleMethodCall(request, response) {
-    var deserializer = new Deserializer()
+    var deserializer = new Deserializer(responseEncoding)
     deserializer.deserializeMethodCall(request, function(error, methodName, params) {
       if (!error && that.listenerCount(methodName) > 0) {
         that.emit(methodName, null, params, function(error, value) {
